course: dictionary
lesson: 9253
title: One word, many meanings: soul
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary can give a word more than one meaning. Soul is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Not a soul was there» is not about a spirit. It means nobody was there.
explain: In religion, the soul is the part of a person that many believers say is their spirit, their feelings and the real "you". «Hindus believe the soul is reborn many times until it reaches freedom, called moksha.» The word "believe" shows this is what people hold to be true.
explain: Soul can also mean deep feeling. «She sings with soul.» The writer does not mean she has a spirit inside her. They mean she sings with great warmth and feeling. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Soul has several meanings, and the context shows you which one is used.
fact: In religion, the soul is the part of a person that many religions believe is spiritual and lives on after death.
fact: «Not a soul» means nobody, and «poor soul» means a person we feel sorry for.
fact: Soul music is a style of African American music with gospel roots.
fact: Different faiths and humanists see the soul differently, so write "Hindus believe..." or "Muslims believe..." rather than stating it as a fact.
exercise: «Not a soul was there when we arrived.» What does soul mean here? | Deep feeling in music | A spirit that lives on after death | *Nobody | A kind of music
exercise: Priya says «Hindus believe the soul is reborn in a new body.» Which word shows this is a belief? | new | *believe | body | reborn
exercise: «She sings with soul.» What does soul mean? | Nobody at all | *Deep feeling and warmth | A type of food | A person's spirit after death
test: «Heart and soul» in a story means what? | *With all your energy | Very quietly | Sleeping | In a religious book
test: «Poor soul» means what? | A bad spirit | A quiet voice | *A person to feel sorry for | A kind of song
exam: Mohammed says Muslims believe the soul waits for the Day of Judgement. Why is it right to write "Muslims believe" instead of "The soul waits"? | Because soul means a body | *Because it is a belief people hold, not a fact everyone agrees on | Because the Day of Judgement has already happened | Because Muslims are the only people who have souls
